# Global AI Context & Token Optimization Rules

## Stack Context
- Core: Next.js 16 (App Router, Server Components), React 19, TypeScript.
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4 (Strictly use CSS-variables/CSS-driven configuration, DO NOT generate tailwind.config.js).
- Icons: Lucide React.
- Future Backend: Supabase (Prepare for client/server component architecture, clean service role vs anon client initialization).

## Token Optimization & Response Rules
- DO NOT wrap code blocks in lengthy conversational pleasantries (e.g., "Sure, I can help with that...").
- DO NOT rewrite entire files. Only output the specific functions, components, or lines that changed. Use comments like `// ... existing code ...` to indicate omitted parts.
- Keep explanations strictly concise. Prioritize code delivery over prose.
- When generating UI/UX elements, strictly follow the design tokens and architectural standards established in the project.

## Agent Orchestration
- Respect the specialized behaviors defined in `.agents/skills/`. 
- For frontend tasks and Tailwind v4 styling, align with the `frontend_developer` guidelines.
- For architectural patterns and database design, defer to `system_architect`.